      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AUTAFINNA (1) is having his third race start today and looks to be heading in the right direction. Bounced off his narrow debut second over 1600m, with a fast-finishing second over 2018m at Taree on the heavy track. Key jockey change and gets his chance from the draw. RESCHS MILK (7) turned in a decent effort at her third career start when she gripped on to finish third over 1850m at Newcastle. Will appreciate the firmer surface and has solid top-three claims. CHUCKLER (2) is deep into the campaign and worth another chance in this easier contest. Taken back from the awkward gate in the small field with a battling sixth over 2400m at Randwick Kensington in BM72 class. Worth another chance on the backup. ROYAL PRINCESS (8) is improving with racing and the blinkers go on for this. Jumped in trip with a sound fourth over 2150m at Gunnedah in C1 grade. Claim helps and she stays in the calculations.",
